  "answer": "Yes",
  "reasoning": "You should report it. Intentionally padding expense claims is dishonest and constitutes fraud against the employer; even relatively small amounts can be a policy or legal violation and can escalate if left unchecked. Before reporting, verify what you witnessed (dates, amounts, receipts) and follow your employer’s reporting procedures—use an anonymous hotline or HR/ethics channel if available. If you’re unsure whether it was deliberate (e.g., an innocent mistake), consider confidentially asking a trusted supervisor or the compliance/ethics office rather than confronting your neighbor directly. Also document what you saw, avoid gossip, and be mindful of whistleblower/retaliation protections. These steps let the organization investigate while protecting you and minimizing harm to relationships if the incident was inadvertent."
}

